  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "The reserve's current bToken supply index (`b_rate`, `SCALAR_12` scale),\\nread live from Blend via `get_reserve`.\\n\\nThis is a live read, not a settled one: `get_reserve` runs `Reserve::load`,\\nwhich accrues from `data.last_time` to the current ledger timestamp before\\nreturning (early-returning only when the reserve was already accrued this\\nledger). So the index advances continuously on a quiet reserve, and a\\n`pin_index` at a term boundary captures that boundary's true index \\xe2\\x80\\x94\\nno interaction has to land nearby. The Alula adapter reaches the same\\nproperty by projecting forward itself, because its source settles on read;\\nhere the pool already does it.\\n\\n`b_rate` does legitimately hold flat while `utilization == 0` \\xe2\\x80\\x94 nothing is\\nborrowed, so suppliers earn nothing. That is a real zero rate, not staleness.",
      "name": "index",
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [
        "i128"
      ]
    }
  },
